Test Architecture and TDD

Tests are written BEFORE implementation. This is not a preference. It is a discipline. Vertical slices, never horizontal.

Write ONE test that confirms ONE thing about the system. This is your tracer bullet: proves the path works end-to-end.

The TDD Vertical Slice

WRONG (horizontal):
  RED:   test1, test2, test3, test4, test5
  GREEN: impl1, impl2, impl3, impl4, impl5

RIGHT (vertical):
  RED→GREEN: test1 → impl1 → pass
  RED→GREEN: test2 → impl2 → pass
  RED→GREEN: test3 → impl3 → pass

