Contract-Driven Development

The golden rule of swarm architecture: swarms must never share mutable state. If two swarms need the same file, one swarm owns it and the other receives a contract. Contracts are ground truth: swarms build against contracts, not each other.

contracts/
  ├── api-types.ts       # All Zod schemas, shared types
  ├── db-schema.md       # Table definitions, relationships
  ├── page-list.md       # All routes, their data needs
  └── adapter-specs.md   # Third-party API interfaces

DISPATCH ORDER:
  Group A: Backend Swarm + Security Swarm (independent)
  Group B: Integration Swarm (needs Group A DB)
  Group C: Frontend Swarm + Polish Swarm (needs Group B API)

