The TDD Swarm Protocol

CYCLE:
  1. DECOMPOSE  → Break task into testable units
  2. TEST-FIRST  → Write tests/specifications (subagent)
  3. IMPLEMENT   → Build to satisfy tests (subagent)
  4. VERIFY      → Run tests against implementation
  5. ITERATE     → On failure: fix, re-verify (repeat until pass)
  6. INTEGRATE   → Merge verified units into final output

PARALLELIZATION RULES:
  Independent units → test and implement IN PARALLEL
  Dependent units   → SEQUENTIAL (bottom-up)
  Use parallel agents when 3+ independent units exist
  Never parallelize units that share mutable state

